nt the memory probe  sequence which features alien Scrolls  flipping back and forth through Carol's  memories like DJs scratching a record or  while providing snarky commentary it was  so odd and entertaining that you barely  noticed the fact it was also serving up  massive amounts of key exposition about  both Carol Danvers and the film's plot  now that's how it's done  with so much information flying up  viewers though it can be easy to get  confused so it doesn't help when the  film was generally confusing like when I  had a hard  I'm explaining its own timeline the film  start of an amnesiac car or living on  the Kree homeworld of hala trying to  land her first mission with the elite  star force commando squad later on  though we discover it's actually been  six years since she was taken from Earth  since she seems like a bit of a rookie  it's jarring as it forces you to ask  just what has she been doing for the  last six years why hasn't she searched  for clues to our past before it's a  minor detail but it pulls you out of the  movie right when you need to be pulled  in as great as brie Larson is in the  title role of the film samuel l.jackson  has been stealing scenes for decades and  Captain Marvel is no exception Jackson  seems to be having a blast as a much  younger more carefree Nick Fury than  were used to seeing less jaded and more  open this fury trades one-liners as  easily as he bonds with the film's other  scene-stealer goofs the cuts this is a  fury would love to see more of  throughout the film a Dumba's is  constantly picked on by a commanding  officer Jude Law's young rogue he and  the other creme repeats over and over  again that she needs to control and  suppress her true self in order to  become what they want her to become  control it's a big metaphor for how  society forces people to conform to  other people's ideals but while the  payoff is ultimately satisfying the  setup doesn't feel organic law often  feels like he's simply reading the 